{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966814,"nonce":"Nz6oKDFdZU+gPAglNCXf+Xq9d4Q=","title":"A computed read inside another computation is stale and untracked","message":"Computed::try_get, called while a computation or effect is running (IN_FLIGHT_GRAPH set), reads through ReactiveGraph::peek_derived (reactive.rs), which returns the cached value: it neither recomputes a dirty derived nor records a dependency. So:\n- a computed built from another computed returns the inner one's stale value after the inner one's signals change, and never re-runs for them;\n- an effect that reads a computed does not re-run when that computed's signals change.\nSolid-style memos compose; here they do not. Signals read in flight are fine (Signal::try_get tracks through g.get).\n\nFix: a reader-side path for in-flight derived reads. A clean derived returns its cached value and adds its dependencies to the reader's tracking; a dirty or never-computed one runs its compute closure against the in-flight graph without caching (compute takes \u0026ReactiveGraph), so its reads land in the reader's tracking. The derived stays dirty, so its next ordinary get recomputes and caches.","files":null}]}